{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EQUAfHvLcxWWYW4fv7z9AV","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Operation Wolfpack\n14:## Contents\n37:## 1. Deliverables and names\n68:## 2. The game in one page\n109:## 3. Research summary: what we keep, what we change\n138:## 4. Genre, perspective, rendering approach\n161:## 5. Controls and prompts\n205:## 6. Architecture and modules\n207:### 6.1 Folder layout (inside the dev folder)\n223:### 6.2 Source files (`src/`, loaded in this order)\n274:### 6.3 Layers and the one rule that keeps them testable\n292:### 6.4 Scenes, flow, deep links\n304:### 6.5 Engine usage and engine changes\n337:### 6.6 Data formats\n382:### 6.7 The debug handle (for the tests and the engine's tools)\n395:## 7. Systems (exact rules and numbers)\n400:### 7.1 Rail camera (`11-rail.js`)\n412:### 7.2 Projection and hit testing (`10-view3d.js`, `12-hit.js`)\n433:### 7.3 Crosshair and aiming (`30-players.js`)\n449:### 7.4 Weapon: the WOLF-9 SMG (`31-weapon.js`)\n467:### 7.5 Grenades and explosions\n483:### 7.6 Enemy AI (`21-infantry.js`, `22-enemyfire.js`)\n516:### 7.7 Projectiles (`23-projectiles.js`)\n531:### 7.8 Vehicles and aircraft (`24-vehicles.js`)\n539:### 7.9 Bosses (`25-bosses.js`)\n546:### 7.10 Player damage, DOWN, continue\n561:### 7.11 Civilians, hostages, animals (`26-friendlies.js`)\n577:### 7.12 Destructibles and cover (`27-props.js`)\n593:### 7.13 Pickups and the supply director (`28-pickups.js`)\n616:### 7.14 Quotas, beats, reinforcements, clear, perks (`33-sim.js`)\n637:### 7.15 Scoring, streaks, ranks, high scores (`32-scoring.js`)\n653:### 7.16 Difficulty and co-op scaling (`01-tuning.js`)\n670:## 8. Content\n672:### 8.1 Setting and cast\n691:### 8.2 Writing style (like the source's)\n699:### 8.3 Story beats and key lines (these exact lines; add more in the same voice)\n736:### 8.4 Bestiary: the Hyena Legion (VETERAN values)\n750:### 8.5 Vehicles, boats, aircraft\n763:### 8.6 The six operations\n771:#### OP 1: RADIO HILL (dawn; teaches everything)\n803:#### OP 2: MANGROVE RUN (misty morning; forward rail on a river)\n832:#### OP 3: PALM VILLAGE (noon; civilians and windows)\n862:#### OP 4: POWDER KEG DEPOT (dusk; explosions)\n890:#### OP 5: THE KENNEL (night and rain; the breakout)\n920:#### OP 6: LAST FLIGHT OUT (sunrise storm; boarding, takeoff, the gunship)\n951:### 8.7 Bosses\n962:### 8.8 Cutscenes (`47-cutscenes.js`)\n980:## 9. Presentation: art assets, animation, audio\n982:### 9.1 Art direction and assets\n1019:### 9.2 Animation (the engine's rig system as the base, plus what this game needs)\n1056:### 9.3 Audio (all in code, no files)\n1102:## 10. UI and UX (10-foot, controller first)\n1104:### 10.1 Rules\n1118:### 10.2 Screens (`71-screens.js`, canvas, pixel art)\n1134:### 10.3 The HUD (`70-hud.js`, the buffer is 480×270)\n1157:### 10.4 Settings (`72-shell.js`, group \"Game\")\n1170:## 11. Dev mode (`73-devmode.js`)\n1175:### 11.1 Live sliders (the important balance variables)\n1207:### 11.2 Toggles, tools and actions\n1225:## 12. Attract mode and the bot\n1227:### 12.1 Attract mode (`81-attract.js`)\n1240:### 12.2 The bot (`80-bot.js`)\n1260:## 13. Multiplayer\n1262:### 13.1 Local co-op (the game on its own)\n1272:### 13.2 AI Hub sessions (`90-net.js`, `91-codec.js`): Session Protocol v1, mode `shared-world`\n1352:## 14. Touch-only devices, About/Credits, exit interview\n1354:### 14.1 Touch-only devices\n1363:### 14.2 About/Credits (`about` scene; the same text goes in the chat reply)\n1384:### 14.3 Exit interview\n1395:## 15. Build order and milestones\n1415:## 16. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1434:## 17. Testing\n1436:### 17.1 The one command\n1449:### 17.2 Suites (what each proves)\n1477:### 17.3 The real AI Hub harness\n1489:### 17.4 Screenshots (only for what a script can't check)\n1500:## 18. Definition of done\n1518 PLAN.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c87f55d5-27de-4595-aefb-732ca102ecfb","uuid":"a19357b9-9fef-42e