6ab-010715e3fe6f\",\"uuid\":\"bb19c400-f8bb-42ea-8298-15870a0da381\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:44:44.809Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"ok\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_016mQTKWuwi14AvEpAQCpzeR\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh3M2ixniM3BWHFbXtxj\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01L78sMc52XE5nNFSaDTyY5J\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":1585,\"limit\":120},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":6997,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":559328,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":6997},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f\",\"uuid\":\"b8b6e0b4-1e3c-4d76-b67f-29e009b56f1f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:44:46.239Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh3M2RN4sjkD11NxWXZQ\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01L78sMc52XE5nNFSaDTyY5J\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":1585,\"limit\":120}}}"," {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01L78sMc52XE5nNFSaDTyY5J\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1585\\t24 × 24 pixel icons (`E.sprite` strings or px drawing, shaded with `E.tones`), each in its §3.4 colour on a dark\\n1586\\trounded tile:\\n1587\\t\\n1588\\t| Icon | Drawing |\\n1589\\t| --- | --- |\\n1590\\t| SWARM | three small rockets fanned |\\n1591\\t| SEEKER | a missile inside a target ring |\\n1592\\t| MINEFIELD | a spiked disc |\\n1593\\t| CANNON | three tracer dashes |\\n1594\\t| RAILSHOT | crosshairs with a long beam to the right |\\n1595\\t| TREMOR | a sine wave over a ground line |\\n1596\\t| BULWARK | a hexagon shield |\\n1597\\t| AUTOPILOT | a steering yoke with an \\\"A\\\" |\\n1598\\t| NITRO | a double flame chevron |\\n1599\\t| SIPHON | a zigzag arrow into a droplet |\\n1600\\t\\n1601\\tThe same icons go on the How to Play pages and in the dev panel's Give weapon. In 3D, the weapon pad's sigil is the\\n1602\\tamber triangle. The HUD shows the icon.\\n1603\\t\\n1604\\t### 4.5 Season events, story beats, academy drills, radio (`08-data-season.js`, `09-data-story.js`)\\n1605\\t\\n1606\\tSpeakers: **ORACLE** (the Authority), **PRINCIPAL** (the player's team's principal), **RIVAL** (`{$rival}`), and\\n1607\\t**PILOT** (`{$pilot}`, the player). Briefings play before an event's first attempt (then from the event tile's\\n1608\\tBRIEFING button). Debriefs play after a result. Each line is one dialog page with a portrait and a gibberish voice.\\n1609\\t✕ advances, △ skips all.\\n1610\\t\\n1611\\t| # | Tier / class | Event | Track | Target (gold / silver / bronze) | Briefing → debrief beats |\\n1612\\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n1613\\t| — | Season open | PROLOGUE (first entry) | — | — | ORACLE: \\\"AUTHORITY NOTICE 0417. ROOKIE LICENCE GRANTED. CLASS: SPARK. GRAVITY: OPTIONAL.\\\" · PRINCIPAL: \\\"Welcome to {$team}. Your test laps were adequate. Adequate is where champions start.\\\" · PRINCIPAL: \\\"Bring back three medals and the Authority lets you go faster.\\\" · RIVAL: \\\"Another rookie. I'll learn your name when I need it for the wreck report.\\\" |\\n1614\\t| E1 | 1 · SPARK | ACADEMY | Port Solenne | all drills first try / ≤ 3 retries / completed | ORACLE: \\\"ELEVEN DRILLS. REPEAT EACH UNTIL COMPLIANT.\\\" → ORACLE: \\\"TRAINING RECORD FILED. YOU MAY NOW RACE OTHER PEOPLE.\\\" |\\n1615\\t| E2 | 1 · SPARK | RACE 3 laps | Port Solenne | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | PRINCIPAL: \\\"Port Solenne. Wide, forgiving, full of yachts. Win, and the sponsors notice.\\\" → win: \\\"First place. The harbour lights flashed our colours. That was contractual.\\\" / podium: \\\"A podium. Keep the trophy dust-free; we photograph it.\\\" / else: \\\"Finishing is a habit. So is losing. Choose.\\\" |\\n1616\\t| E3 | 1 · SPARK | TIME TRIAL 3 laps | Karakum Spire | medal times | PRINCIPAL: \\\"No weapons, no excuses. The gorge wants two hundred and seventy kilometres an hour. Arrive with them.\\\" → \\\"The clock has accepted your apology.\\\" |\\n1617\\t| E4 | 1 · SPARK | RACE 3 laps | Karakum Spire | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | RIVAL: \\\"Karakum has a gorge. Most rookies meet the bottom of it.\\\" · PRINCIPAL: \\\"Ignore {$rival}. Take the speed pads before the ramp.\\\" → win: RIVAL: \\\"Luck. Statistically you're due a wall.\\\" |\\n1618\\t| — | tier 1 done (3 medals) | PROMOTION | — | — | ORACLE: \\\"AUTHORITY NOTICE 0533. PILOT {$pilot} PROMOTED. CLASS: FLARE.\\\" · PRINCIPAL: \\\"They noticed you. That is not always good.\\\" (unlocks FLARE) |\\n1619\\t| E5 | 2 · FLARE | SNIPEOUT first to 10 | Meridian Stack | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | PRINCIPAL: \\\"Snipeout. A point for every hit, three for every elimination. In the Stack, everyone is a target.\\\" · RIVAL: \\\"Stand still. It's more efficient.\\\" → \\\"Sniped clean. The Stack's residents filed noise complaints.\\\" |\\n1620\\t| E6 | 2 · FLARE | OVERCLOCK | Port Solenne | zone 30 / 20 / 10 | ORACLE: \\\"INVESTIGATION 77-B: UNSANCTIONED OVERCLOCKING. ALL PILOTS WILL DEMONSTRATE COMPLIANCE.\\\" · PRINCIPAL: \\\"{$rivalTeam} has been running engines hot. The Authority wants to see what an honest engine survives. Show them.\\\" → ORACLE: \\\"COMPLIANCE NOTED. ZONE {$zone}.\\\" |\\n1621\\t| E7 | 2 · FLARE | HOT LAP | Meridian Stack | medal lap times | PRINCIPAL: \\\"One perfect lap. Our sponsor's board meets tomorrow. Give them a number.\\\" → \\\"They framed the number. Literally.\\\" |\\n1622\\t| E8 | 2 · FLARE | RACE 3 laps | Meridian Stack | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | PRINCIPAL: \\\"QWIK-FUEL wants a podium at Meridian, or they paint someone else's craft. No pressure. Some pressure.\\\" → podium: \\\"QWIK-FUEL renewed. We are once again flammable.\\\" |\\n1623\\t| — | tier 2 done | PROMOTION | — | — | ORACLE: \\\"AUTHORITY NOTICE 0610. CLASS: STORM. PILOTS ARE REMINDED THAT WALLS DO NOT MOVE.\\\" · RIVAL: \\\"Storm class. Finally, something fast enough to be interesting.\\\" (unlocks STORM) |\\n1624\\t| E9 | 3 · STORM | RACE 3 laps | Borealis Vault | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | PRINCIPAL: \\\"Borealis. Cold, long, and the Vault is seventeen metres straight down. Land it flat.\\\" → \\\"You came back warmer than you left.\\\" |\\n1625\\t| E10 | 3 · STORM | SNIPEOUT first to 12 | Karakum Spire | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | RIVAL: \\\"Rematch in the canyon. Bring a shield. Bring two.\\\" → win: RIVAL: \\\"Fine. The Grand Prix, then.\\\" |\\n1626\\t| — | E9 + E10 medalled | GP UNLOCK | — | — | ORACLE: \\\"THE HOVERLINE GRAND PRIX. FOUR CIRCUITS. ONE CHAMPION. SPECTATORS ARE ADVISED TO REMAIN BEHIND THE BARRIERS.\\\" |\\n1627\\t| GP | final · STORM | 4 races × 3 laps: Solenne → Karakum → Meridian → Borealis, points 10-8-6-5-4-3-2-1 | all | champion / 2nd / 3rd overall | between races: ORACLE reads the standings: \\\"LEADER: {$leader}. GAP: {$gap} POINTS.\\\" Then a PRINCIPAL or RIVAL line by situation (leading / chasing / behind; 2 each) |\\n1628\\t| END | — | ENDING (any GP medal) | hangar podium | — | champion: ORACLE: \\\"AUTHORITY NOTICE 0700. CHAMPION: {$pilot}, {$team}. SINGULARITY CLASS AUTHORISED.\\\" · PRINCIPAL: \\\"Champion. I prepared a speech. I'll skip it.\\\" · RIVAL: \\\"Enjoy it. Next season, I'm faster.\\\" · ORACLE: \\\"THE AUTHORITY REMINDS ALL PILOTS: GRAVITY IS OPTIONAL. CONTRACTS ARE NOT.\\\" → the credits roll (About page 5) over a hangar podium orbit. Podium variant: PRINCIPAL: \\\"A Grand Prix podium. The board calls it progress. I call it next year.\\\" (SINGULARITY unlocks on any GP medal; the CHAMPION livery needs gold) |\\n1629\\t\\n1630\\t**Academy drills** (E1, and ACADEMY in the menu). Each drill:\\n1631\\t- teleports the player to its start (`s`, `u`, a speed);\\n1632\\t- shows a big instruction card with **live glyphs** (`{thrust}` becomes ✕, W or a mouse icon by device);\\n1633\\t- checks success;\\n1634\\t- on failure: \\\"TRY AGAIN\\\" and a reset after 2 s;\\n1635\\t- on success: \\\"DRILL CLEAR\\\" plus a chime.\\n1636\\t\\n1637\\tThe instructor is ORACLE. The track is Port Solenne at SPARK, solo.\\n1638\\t\\n1639\\t| # | Drill | Start | Instruction (with glyph tokens) | Success check |\\n1640\\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n1641\\t| 1 | THRUST | grid | \\\"Hold {thrust} to thrust. Reach 250 km/h.\\\" | speed ≥ 250 km/h |\\n1642\\t| 2 | STEER | cp1 + 60 m | \\\"Steer with {steer} through the three gates.\\\" | pass 3 holo-gates (rings at u = −6, +6, −6 m, 80 m apart) within ±3 m |\\n1643\\t| 3 | AIRBRAKES | cp18 − 150 m, 220 km/h | \\\"Squeeze {brakeL} or {brakeR} through the lighthouse hairpin. Stay off the walls.\\\" | an airbrake > 0.3 held ≥ 0.5 s in the hairpin, no wall hit, exit ≥ 150 km/h |\\n1644\\t| 4 | PITCH | cp10 + 0 m (the old-town descent, about −5 %), 200 km/h | \\\"Downhill: hold {noseDown} to pitch the nose down and gain speed.\\\" | pitch ≥ 0.5 for 1 s on the descent, and +15 km/h |\\n1645\\t| 5 | SPEED PADS | cp16 − 100 m | \\\"Blue chevrons boost you. Hit two speed pads.\\\" | 2 speed-pad events (cp16 and cp21 pads) |\\n1646\\t| 6 | WEAPONS | cp2 − 100 m | \\\"Amber pads arm you. Collect a weapon, then fire {fire} at the target drone.\\\" | a forced SWARM pickup; the TARGET DRONE (a hovering ring craft, 30 HP, on track at cp3) hit ≥ 1 |\\n1647\\t| 7 | ABSORB | cp11 − 100 m | \\\"Not every weapon is worth firing. Collect one and absorb it with {absorb}.\\\" | a forced MINEFIELD pickup, then an absorb event (energy goes up) |\\n1648\\t| 8 | SIDE-SHIFT | cp15 − 200 m | \\\"Mines ahead. Side-shift with {shiftL} or {shiftR} to slip past.\\\" | a mine line (3 mines spanning 2/3 of the width, the gap on the far side) passed with no hit and a side-shift used in the last 1.5 s |\\n1649\\t| 9 | BARREL ROLL | cp11 + 50 m, at 300 km/h | \\\"Off the Harbour Step, flick {steer} left-right, or press {shiftL}/{shiftR} in the air. Land the roll for a boost.\\\" | a `roll` event with `ok` |\\n1650\\t| 10 | PIT LANE | cp21 + 0 m, energy 40 % | \\\"Shield low. Ride the green pit strip to recharge to full.\\\" | energy ≥ 99 |\\n1651\\t| 11 | FULL LAP | grid, standing start | \\\"Put it together. One lap under sixty seconds.\\\" | a lap ≤ 60.0 s at SPARK (the ideal line is about 46 s) |\\n1652\\t\\n1653\\t\\n1654\\t**Race radio:** a pool of about 30 short lines, gibberish plus subtitle in the radio box, rate-limited to one per\\n1655\\t12 s. Triggers: overtaking or being overtaken by a named pilot, a weapon hit, an elimination, the final lap. Speakers\\n1656\\tare the pilots (§4.1 banter, plus 2 more each), for example:\\n1657\\t- \\\"Make room.\\\" / \\\"Too slow, rookie.\\\" / \\\"That one stung.\\\" / \\\"Shield's holding.\\\" / \\\"Pit lane, now.\\\" (own team)\\n1658\\t- RIVAL: \\\"Behind you. Still.\\\" / \\\"Smile for the wreck report.\\\"\\n1659\\t\\n1660\\t### 4.6 Sponsors and signage (`66-scenery.js` canvas textures)\\n1661\\t\\n1662\\tFictional brands for gantries, billboards, wall panels and holograms. Each is a logo (a geometric mark drawn in px)\\n1663\\tplus a name and a slogan, in the engine's pixel font at scale 2–4 on 128–256 px canvases:\\n1664\\t\\n1665\\t| Brand | Slogan |\\n1666\\t| --- | --- |\\n1667\\t| QWIK-FUEL | FILL UP. FALL UP. |\\n1668\\t| OKTA NOODLE | EAT AT 600 KM/H |\\n1669\\t| HALCYON BANK | YOUR MONEY, FASTER |\\n1670\\t| AXON AIR | BREATHE PREMIUM |\\n1671\\t| VANTA PAINTS | DARKER THAN NOTHING |\\n1672\\t| MERIDIAN TELECOM | ALWAYS ON. ALWAYS. |\\n1673\\t| POLARIS COLD STORAGE | WE KEEP IT FROM YOU |\\n1674\\t| NOVA-CHROME | SHINE RESPONSIBLY |\\n1675\\t| KIBO TEA | STEEPED IN THE FUTURE |\\n1676\\t| ORBIT SOCKS | KEEP YOUR FEET IN ORBIT |\\n1677\\t| THE AUTHORITY | DO NOT LOOK DIRECTLY AT THE FUTURE |\\n1678\\t| SOLENNE TOURISM | COME FOR THE SEA. STAY FOR THE SPEED. |\\n1679\\t\\n1680\\tSignage: SECTOR markers 1–8, PIT, the jump warnings (\\\"GORGE: 270 KM/H MINIMUM\\\"), and chevron boards.\\n1681\\t\\n1682\\t---\\n1683\\t\\n1684\\t## 5. Build order and milestones\\n1685\\t\\n1686\\tThe ordering principle: **the riskiest unknown first**. First the 3D stack in one file, then the core loop (one craft\\n1687\\ton one track), then a full race (AI and weapons). Breadth comes after that (modes, UI, season, audio), then\\n1688\\tintegration (attract, dev, hub). Polish is last. Each milestone ends with its tests passing in `node tests/run.mjs`.\\n1689\\t\\n1690\\t| # | Milestone | Deliverables | Exit tests (all automated unless marked 📷 = screenshot review) |\\n1691\\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n1692\\t| **M0** | Skeleton and stack spike | Dev folder, pinned downloads (§2.1), `package.json`, `tests/run.mjs` and `tests/lib/vm.mjs`, `tools/bundle.mjs`, `index.html`. A minimal `95-main.js`: `new E.Game` with SN.INPUT, the boot steps (the 3D wait/init), a test oval TrackDef rendered as a plain ribbon mesh in a terrain world, a dummy craft box moving along it at 2000 u/s, the chase cam, an overlay text | Node: the game boots headless and `advance(5)` runs with no errors. Browser: the bundle opens from file:// with no page errors; `World3D.backend` is 'WebGPU' or 'WebGL 2'; the #view canvas is non-black over > 30 % of its area; it reaches race view in < 15 s. 📷 the ribbon and box |\\n1693\\t| **M1** | Tracks | `20-track.js` complete: spline, slices, frames, bank, features, surface, locate, query, line, speed profile, validation, minimap. `07-data-tracks.js` with all 4 tracks. `tools/trackcheck.mjs` | unit: frame handedness (8 headings), bank sign, closure continuity (`C(L−ε) ≈ C(0)`), arc-length error < 0.1 %, lengths within 1 % of §4.3, overpass clearances (24.5 / 31.9 m ±0.5), the `{cp,d}` feature s-values, the racing line inside the bounds, speed profile ≤ top. 📷 an overhead debug render of each track with features |\\n1694\\t| **M2** | One craft that flies right | `25-ship.js`, `27-collide.js` (bodies only), `01-input.js` (mapping, double tap, flick, vpad), Tune registry, engine edits §2.7.1–3 (glyphs default, font glyphs, analog values) and §2.7.5. A player craft on any track, keyboard and pad | physics suite (§7.2): the feel targets of §3.2, walls never crossed at 3000 u/s, no NaN in 10 min of random input, the jumps per App. C at each class, drop landings, overpass stability (s never jumps levels), pads, pit, side-shift lateral 3–5 m, the barrel-roll boost and botch, rescue after a fall, the centre-line bot laps every track × class with 0 rescues |\\n1695\\t| **M3** | It looks like the game | `60-render.js` (worlds, interpolation, cameras), `64-trackmesh.js` (surface, walls with neon and chevrons, pads, tunnels, supports, gantries, drop and gap faces), `62-shipkit.js` (6 craft, liveries, flaps, glow, trails, roll), the themes' sky/fog/sun and terrain carve, basic scenery per theme, bloom | browser: each track loads in < 10 s; no shader stalls over 50 ms after GO (frame-time log); 📷 per track: the start grid, a banked corner (roll sign), a tunnel, the jump, the overpass from both decks; all 6 craft on the turntable |\\n1696\\t| **M4** | A real race | `40-race.js` (lifecycle, grid, countdown and launch revs, laps, sectors, positions, wrong way, finish, results, elimination), `35-ai.js` (line, speed, control, avoidance, pads, mistakes, rubber band, difficulty), `45-replay.js` (record and replay, hash) | race suite: an 8-AI race on every track × class finishes; no craft stuck > 3 s; ≤ 1 rescue per craft per race; lap times within ±25 % of §4.2; positions consistent with progress; `hash` equal on two runs from the same seed; a replay re-sim gives an equal hash; wrong-way detection; the launch-boost window |\\n1697\\t| **M5** | Combat | `30-weapons.js` (pads, roll table, 10 weapons, absorb, lock-on, damage, stagger), AI weapon logic, `68-fx.js` for every weapon, events wired to placeholder-free SFX (simple `audio.define` voices at first, final ones in M9) | weapons suite: each weapon fired by a scripted craft at a target in a fixed setup deals its damage; the target's warning appears; BULWARK blocks; absorb adds energy; MINEFIELD triggers; TREMOR misses airborne craft; SIPHON transfers; RAILSHOT hits within its aim tolerance and misses outside; elimination at 0 (DNF in a race, respawn in SNIPEOUT); in an 8-AI race every weapon is used at least once across 4 seeded races |\\n1698\\t| **M6** | HUD and front-end | `70-hud.js`, `55-glyphs.js`, `75-ui.js` (widget kit, every §3.9 screen), settings (§3.17), pause items, the touch-only notice, the About skeleton | flow suite: title → menu → quick race setup → loading → race → results → menu by scripted taps; mouse hover focus (`input.feed('move')`) and click activation; the prompt bar switches device (key, pad stub, mouse); Button symbols switches PS ↔ Xbox labels; the touch-only notice when `matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)')` is false and `maxTouchPoints > 0` (stubbed in vm), with no touch buttons (`input.touchButtons` never called). 📷 every screen at 1280×720 and 1920×1080 |\\n1699\\t| **M7** | Every mode | TIME TRIAL plus ghosts, HOT LAP, SNIPEOUT, OVERCLOCK plus the skin, ACADEMY (11 drills, drone, gates, mine line), VERSUS (join, half keys, split HUD), the REPLAY scene, records | modes suite: each mode starts, plays, and ends with correct results; ghost save/load round-trips and plays back aligned (< 1 m error); Overclock zones advance and the run ends at 0 energy; the academy bot passes all drills; versus with 2 inputs makes 2 viewports and both finish; replay click-to-follow selects the clicked craft (feed a click at a projected position) |\\n1700\\t| **M8** | Season and story | `08-data-season.js`, `09-data-story.js`, `78-season-ui.js` (hub, briefings, GP, ending, credits), saves, unlocks | season suite: the **scripted playthrough** (§7.4) of the whole season with the player bot; unlocks fire in order; save → reload → state equal; every dialog line references only defined vars; every event playable |\\n1701\\t| **M9** | Sound | engine edit §2.7.4; `50-audio.js`: 6 songs and stings, the full SFX catalogue, engine hums, the music director (layers, final lap, overclock tempo), `SN.Voice` gibberish, announcer callouts, radio | audio suite (headless, no WebAudio): every song parses with no engine warnings and is ≥ 16 bars; each event type maps to an existing sound; `Voice.say` durations are > 0 and stable per word; the music layers react to race events (`audio.pos.layers`). 🔊 a human-free check: in the browser, record `audio.drift` stays < 10 ms and no audio errors |\\n1702\\t| **M10** | Attract and dev | `85-attract.js`, `80-dev.js` (panel, cheats, sliders, reset, overlays, info) | flow: 10.0 s idle on the title → attract starts (not at 9.9 s); any of key/pad/click exits within 1 step; the attract shows ≥ 8 distinct weapons and ≥ 3 tracks across one loop (counted from events); dev: every slider changes `SN.Tune.T` and the sim responds (e.g., topSpeedMul 1.5 raises top speed); RESET ALL restores every default exactly; each cheat works |\\n1703\\t| **M11** | AI Hub | `90-hub.js`, its own card, ghost send/receive, the session scene | hub suite (Node mock of `AIHub`, §7.6) and the **real harness** (§7.6): `players=2&auto=1`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, `…&scenario=host-leave`; `__hubCheck.pass === true` in each |\\n1704\\t| **M12** | Polish and ship | scenery density, effects, juice (shake, flashes, rumble via `input.rumble`), the balance pass with the sliders, medal calibration (`tools/medals.mjs`), the About pages filled, `exit-interview.json`, the final bundle | the full `node tests/run.mjs` passes; `tools/bundle.mjs` passes its checks (no TODO, an identical hub client); `node engine/handoff/tools/check.mjs ../<bundle>.html` gives no errors (it will list the CDN files as external, which is expected); 📷 the final screenshot set (§7.7) |\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f\",\"uuid\":\"1708212a-72f7-46f8-b670-a648a3d274b4\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:44:46.244Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md\",\"content\":\"24 × 24 pixel icons (`E.sprite` strings or px drawing, shaded with `E.tones`), each in its §3.4 colour on a dark\\nrounded tile:\\n\\n| Icon | Drawing |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| SWARM | three small rockets fanned |\\n| SEEKER | a missile inside a target ring |\\n| MINEFIELD | a spiked disc |\\n| CANNON | three tracer dashes |\\n| RAILSHOT | crosshairs with a long beam to the right |\\n| TREMOR | a sine wave over a ground line |\\n| BULWARK | a hexagon shield |\\n| AUTOPILOT | a steering yoke with an \\\"A\\\" |\\n| NITRO | a double flame chevron |\\n| SIPHON | a zigzag arrow into a droplet |\\n\\nThe same icons go on the How to Play pages and in the dev panel's Give weapon. In 3D, the weapon pad's sigil is the\\namber triangle. The HUD shows the icon.\\n\\n### 4.5 Season events, story beats, academy drills, radio (`08-data-season.js`, `09-data-story.js`)\\n\\nSpeakers: **ORACLE** (the Authority), **PRINCIPAL** (the player's team's principal), **RIVAL** (`{$rival}`), and\\n**PILOT** (`{$pilot}`, the player). Briefings play before an event's first attempt (then from the event tile's\\nBRIEFING button). Debriefs play after a result. Each line is one dialog page with a portrait and a gibberish voice.\\n✕ advances, △ skips all.\\n\\n| # | Tier / class | Event | Track | Target (gold / silver / bronze) | Briefing → debrief beats |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| — | Season open | PROLOGUE (first entry) | — | — | ORACLE: \\\"AUTHORITY NOTICE 0417. ROOKIE LICENCE GRANTED. CLASS: SPARK. GRAVITY: OPTIONAL.\\\" · PRINCIPAL: \\\"Welcome to {$team}. Your test laps were adequate. Adequate is where champions start.\\\" · PRINCIPAL: \\\"Bring back three medals and the Authority lets you go faster.\\\" · RIVAL: \\\"Another rookie. I'll learn your name when I need it for the wreck report.\\\" |\\n| E1 | 1 · SPARK | ACADEMY | Port Solenne | all drills first try / ≤ 3 retries / completed | ORACLE: \\\"ELEVEN DRILLS. REPEAT EACH UNTIL COMPLIANT.\\\" → ORACLE: \\\"TRAINING RECORD FILED. YOU MAY NOW RACE OTHER PEOPLE.\\\" |\\n| E2 | 1 · SPARK | RACE 3 laps | Port Solenne | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | PRINCIPAL: \\\"Port Solenne. Wide, forgiving, full of yachts. Win, and the sponsors notice.\\\" → win: \\\"First place. The harbour lights flashed our colours. That was contractual.\\\" / podium: \\\"A podium. Keep the trophy dust-free; we photograph it.\\\" / else: \\\"Finishing is a habit. So is losing. Choose.\\\" |\\n| E3 | 1 · SPARK | TIME TRIAL 3 laps | Karakum Spire | medal times | PRINCIPAL: \\\"No weapons, no excuses. The gorge wants two hundred and seventy kilometres an hour. Arrive with them.\\\" → \\\"The clock has accepted your apology.\\\" |\\n| E4 | 1 · SPARK | RACE 3 laps | Karakum Spire | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | RIVAL: \\\"Karakum has a gorge. Most rookies meet the bottom of it.\\\" · PRINCIPAL: \\\"Ignore {$rival}. Take the speed pads before the ramp.\\\" → win: RIVAL: \\\"Luck. Statistically you're due a wall.\\\" |\\n| — | tier 1 done (3 medals) | PROMOTION | — | — | ORACLE: \\\"AUTHORITY NOTICE 0533. PILOT {$pilot} PROMOTED. CLASS: FLARE.\\\" · PRINCIPAL: \\\"They noticed you. That is not always good.\\\" (unlocks FLARE) |\\n| E5 | 2 · FLARE | SNIPEOUT first to 10 | Meridian Stack | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | PRINCIPAL: \\\"Snipeout. A point for every hit, three for every elimination. In the Stack, everyone is a target.\\\" · RIVAL: \\\"Stand still. It's more efficient.\\\" → \\\"Sniped clean. The Stack's residents filed noise complaints.\\\" |\\n| E6 | 2 · FLARE | OVERCLOCK | Port Solenne | zone 30 / 20 / 10 | ORACLE: \\\"INVESTIGATION 77-B: UNSANCTIONED OVERCLOCKING. ALL PILOTS WILL DEMONSTRATE COMPLIANCE.\\\" · PRINCIPAL: \\\"{$rivalTeam} has been running engines hot. The Authority wants to see what an honest engine survives. Show them.\\\" → ORACLE: \\\"COMPLIANCE NOTED. ZONE {$zone}.\\\" |\\n| E7 | 2 · FLARE | HOT LAP | Meridian Stack | medal lap times | PRINCIPAL: \\\"One perfect lap. Our sponsor's board meets tomorrow. Give them a number.\\\" → \\\"They framed the number. Literally.\\\" |\\n| E8 | 2 · FLARE | RACE 3 laps | Meridian Stack | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | PRINCIPAL: \\\"QWIK-FUEL wants a podium at Meridian, or they paint someone else's craft. No pressure. Some pressure.\\\" → podium: \\\"QWIK-FUEL renewed. We are once again flammable.\\\" |\\n| — | tier 2 done | PROMOTION | — | — | ORACLE: \\\"AUTHORITY NOTICE 0610. CLASS: STORM. PILOTS ARE REMINDED THAT WALLS DO NOT MOVE.\\\" · RIVAL: \\\"Storm class. Finally, something fast enough to be interesting.\\\" (unlocks STORM) |\\n| E9 | 3 · STORM | RACE 3 laps | Borealis Vault | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | PRINCIPAL: \\\"Borealis. Cold, long, and the Vault is seventeen metres straight down. Land it flat.\\\" → \\\"You came back warmer than you left.\\\" |\\n| E10 | 3 · STORM | SNIPEOUT first to 12 | Karakum Spire | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | RIVAL: \\\"Rematch in the canyon. Bring a shield. Bring two.\\\" → win: RIVAL: \\\"Fine. The Grand Prix, then.\\\" |\\n| — | E9 + E10 medalled | GP UNLOCK | — | — | ORACLE: \\\"THE HOVERLINE GRAND PRIX. FOUR CIRCUITS. ONE CHAMPION. SPECTATORS ARE ADVISED TO REMAIN BEHIND THE BARRIERS.\\\" |\\n| GP | final · STORM | 4 races × 3 laps: Solenne → Karakum → Meridian → Borealis, points 10-8-6-5-4-3-2-1 | all | champion / 2nd / 3rd overall | between races: ORACLE reads the standings: \\\"LEADER: {$leader}. GAP: {$gap} POINTS.\\\" Then a PRINCIPAL or RIVAL line by situation (leading / chasing / behind; 2 each) |\\n| END | — | ENDING (any GP medal) | hangar podium | — | champion: ORACLE: \\\"AUTHORITY NOTICE 0700. CHAMPION: {$pilot}, {$team}. SINGULARITY CLASS AUTHORISED.\\\" · PRINCIPAL: \\\"Champion. I prepared a speech. I'll skip it.\\\" · RIVAL: \\\"Enjoy it. Next season, I'm faster.\\\" · ORACLE: \\\"THE AUTHORITY REMINDS ALL PILOTS: GRAVITY IS OPTIONAL. CONTRACTS ARE NOT.\\\" → the credits roll (About page 5) over a hangar podium orbit. Podium variant: PRINCIPAL: \\\"A Grand Prix podium. The board calls it progress. I call it next year.\\\" (SINGULARITY unlocks on any GP medal; the CHAMPION livery needs gold) |\\n\\n**Academy drills** (E1, and ACADEMY in the menu). Each drill:\\n- teleports the player to its start (`s`, `u`, a speed);\\n- shows a big instruction card with **live glyphs** (`{thrust}` becomes ✕, W or a mouse icon by device);\\n- checks success;\\n- on failure: \\\"TRY AGAIN\\\" and a reset after 2 s;\\n- on success: \\\"DRILL CLEAR\\\" plus a chime.\\n\\nThe instructor is ORACLE. The track is Port Solenne at SPARK, solo.\\n\\n| # | Drill | Start | Instruction (with glyph tokens) | Success check |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| 1 | THRUST | grid | \\\"Hold {thrust} to thrust. Reach 250 km/h.\\\" | speed ≥ 250 km/h |\\n| 2 | STEER | cp1 + 60 m | \\\"Steer with {steer} through the three gates.\\\" | pass 3 holo-gates (rings at u = −6, +6, −6 m, 80 m apart) within ±3 m |\\n| 3 | AIRBRAKES | cp18 − 150 m, 220 km/h | \\\"Squeeze {brakeL} or {brakeR} through the lighthouse hairpin. Stay off the walls.\\\" | an airbrake > 0.3 held ≥ 0.5 s in the hairpin, no wall hit, exit ≥ 150 km/h |\\n| 4 | PITCH | cp10 + 0 m (the old-town descent, about −5 %), 200 km/h | \\\"Downhill: hold {noseDown} to pitch the nose down and gain speed.\\\" | pitch ≥ 0.5 for 1 s on the descent, and +15 km/h |\\n| 5 | SPEED PADS | cp16 − 100 m | \\\"Blue chevrons boost you. Hit two speed pads.\\\" | 2 speed-pad events (cp16 and cp21 pads) |\\n| 6 | WEAPONS | cp2 − 100 m | \\\"Amber pads arm you. Collect a weapon, then fire {fire} at the target drone.\\\" | a forced SWARM pickup; the TARGET DRONE (a hovering ring craft, 30 HP, on track at cp3) hit ≥ 1 |\\n| 7 | ABSORB | cp11 − 100 m | \\\"Not every weapon is worth firing. Collect one and absorb it with {absorb}.\\\" | a forced MINEFIELD pickup, then an absorb event (energy goes up) |\\n| 8 | SIDE-SHIFT | cp15 − 200 m | \\\"Mines ahead. Side-shift with {shiftL} or {shiftR} to slip past.\\\" | a mine line (3 mines spanning 2/3 of the width, the gap on the far side) passed with no hit and a side-shift used in the last 1.5 s |\\n| 9 | BARREL ROLL | cp11 + 50 m, at 300 km/h | \\\"Off the Harbour Step, flick {steer} left-right, or press {shiftL}/{shiftR} in the air. Land the roll for a boost.\\\" | a `roll` event with `ok` |\\n| 10 | PIT LANE | cp21 + 0 m, energy 40 % | \\\"Shield low. Ride the green pit strip to recharge to full.\\\" | energy ≥ 99 |\\n| 11 | FULL LAP | grid, standing start | \\\"Put it together. One lap under sixty seconds.\\\" | a lap ≤ 60.0 s at SPARK (the ideal line is about 46 s) |\\n\\n\\n**Race radio:** a pool of about 30 short lines, gibberish plus subtitle in the radio box, rate-limited to one per\\n12 s. Triggers: overtaking or being overtaken by a named pilot, a weapon hit, an elimination, the final lap. Speakers\\nare the pilots (§4.1 banter, plus 2 more each), for example:\\n- \\\"Make room.\\\" / \\\"Too slow, rookie.\\\" / \\\"That one stung.\\\" / \\\"Shield's holding.\\\" / \\\"Pit lane, now.\\\" (own team)\\n- RIVAL: \\\"Behind you. Still.\\\" / \\\"Smile for the wreck report.\\\"\\n\\n### 4.6 Sponsors and signage (`66-scenery.js` canvas textures)\\n\\nFictional brands for gantries, billboards, wall panels and holograms. Each is a logo (a geometric mark drawn in px)\\nplus a name and a slogan, in the engine's pixel font at scale 2–4 on 128–256 px canvases:\\n\\n| Brand | Slogan |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| QWIK-FUEL | FILL UP. FALL UP. |\\n| OKTA NOODLE | EAT AT 600 KM/H |\\n| HALCYON BANK | YOUR MONEY, FASTER |\\n| AXON AIR | BREATHE PREMIUM |\\n| VANTA PAINTS | DARKER THAN NOTHING |\\n| MERIDIAN TELECOM | ALWAYS ON. ALWAYS. |\\n| POLARIS COLD STORAGE | WE KEEP IT FROM YOU |\\n| NOVA-CHROME | SHINE RESPONSIBLY |\\n| KIBO TEA | STEEPED IN THE FUTURE |\\n| ORBIT SOCKS | KEEP YOUR FEET IN ORBIT |\\n| THE AUTHORITY | DO NOT LOOK DIRECTLY AT THE FUTURE |\\n| SOLENNE TOURISM | COME FOR THE SEA. STAY FOR THE SPEED. |\\n\\nSignage: SECTOR markers 1–8, PIT, the jump warnings (\\\"GORGE: 270 KM/H MINIMUM\\\"), and chevron boards.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Build order and milestones\\n\\nThe ordering principle: **the riskiest unknown first**. First the 3D stack in one file, then the core loop (one craft\\non one track), then a full race (AI and weapons). Breadth comes after that (modes, UI, season, audio), then\\nintegration (attract, dev, hub). Polish is last. Each milestone ends with its tests passing in `node tests/run.mjs`.\\n\\n| # | Milestone | Deliverables | Exit tests (all automated unless marked 📷 = screenshot review) |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| **M0** | Skeleton and stack spike | Dev folder, pinned downloads (§2.1), `package.json`, `tests/run.mjs` and `tests/lib/vm.mjs`, `tools/bundle.mjs`, `index.html`. A minimal `95-main.js`: `new E.Game` with SN.INPUT, the boot steps (the 3D wait/init), a test oval TrackDef rendered as a plain ribbon mesh in a terrain world, a dummy craft box moving along it at 2000 u/s, the chase cam, an overlay text | Node: the game boots headless and `advance(5)` runs with no errors. Browser: the bundle opens from file:// with no page errors; `World3D.backend` is 'WebGPU' or 'WebGL 2'; the #view canvas is non-black over > 30 % of its area; it reaches race view in < 15 s. 📷 the ribbon and box |\\n| **M1** | Tracks | `20-track.js` complete: spline, slices, frames, bank, features, surface, locate, query, line, speed profile, validation, minimap. `07-data-tracks.js` with all 4 tracks. `tools/trackcheck.mjs` | unit: frame handedness (8 headings), bank sign, closure continuity (`C(L−ε) ≈ C(0)`), arc-length error < 0.1 %, lengths within 1 % of §4.3, overpass clearances (24.5 / 31.9 m ±0.5), the `{cp,d}` feature s-values, the racing line inside the bounds, speed profile ≤ top. 📷 an overhead debug render of each track with features |\\n| **M2** | One craft that flies right | `25-ship.js`, `27-collide.js` (bodies only), `01-input.js` (mapping, double tap, flick, vpad), Tune registry, engine edits §2.7.1–3 (glyphs default, font glyphs, analog values) and §2.7.5. A player craft on any track, keyboard and pad | physics suite (§7.2): the feel targets of §3.2, walls never crossed at 3000 u/s, no NaN in 10 min of random input, the jumps per App. C at each class, drop landings, overpass stability (s never jumps levels), pads, pit, side-shift lateral 3–5 m, the barrel-roll boost and botch, rescue after a fall, the centre-line bot laps every track × class with 0 rescues |\\n| **M3** | It looks like the game | `60-render.js` (worlds, interpolation, cameras), `64-trackmesh.js` (surface, walls with neon and chevrons, pads, tunnels, supports, gantries, drop and gap faces), `62-shipkit.js` (6 craft, liveries, flaps, glow, trails, roll), the themes' sky/fog/sun and terrain carve, basic scenery per theme, bloom | browser: each track loads in < 10 s; no shader stalls over 50 ms after GO (frame-time log); 📷 per track: the start grid, a banked corner (roll sign), a tunnel, the jump, the overpass from both decks; all 6 craft on the turntable |\\n| **M4** | A real race | `40-race.js` (lifecycle, grid, countdown and launch revs, laps, sectors, positions, wrong way, finish, results, elimination), `35-ai.js` (line, speed, control, avoidance, pads, mistakes, rubber band, difficulty), `45-replay.js` (record and replay, hash) | race suite: an 8-AI race on every track × class finishes; no craft stuck > 3 s; ≤ 1 rescue per craft per race; lap times within ±25 % of §4.2; positions consistent with progress; `hash` equal on two runs from the same seed; a replay re-sim gives an equal hash; wrong-way detection; the launch-boost window |\\n| **M5** | Combat | `30-weapons.js` (pads, roll table, 10 weapons, absorb, lock-on, damage, stagger), AI weapon logic, `68-fx.js` for every weapon, events wired to placeholder-free SFX (simple `audio.define` voices at first, final ones in M9) | weapons suite: each weapon fired by a scripted craft at a target in a fixed setup deals its damage; the target's warning appears; BULWARK blocks; absorb adds energy; MINEFIELD triggers; TREMOR misses airborne craft; SIPHON transfers; RAILSHOT hits within its aim tolerance and misses outside; elimination at 0 (DNF in a race, respawn in SNIPEOUT); in an 8-AI race every weapon is used at least once across 4 seeded races |\\n| **M6** | HUD and front-end | `70-hud.js`, `55-glyphs.js`, `75-ui.js` (widget kit, every §3.9 screen), settings (§3.17), pause items, the touch-only notice, the About skeleton | flow suite: title → menu → quick race setup → loading → race → results → menu by scripted taps; mouse hover focus (`input.feed('move')`) and click activation; the prompt bar switches device (key, pad stub, mouse); Button symbols switches PS ↔ Xbox labels; the touch-only notice when `matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)')` is false and `maxTouchPoints > 0` (stubbed in vm), with no touch buttons (`input.touchButtons` never called). 📷 every screen at 1280×720 and 1920×1080 |\\n| **M7** | Every mode | TIME TRIAL plus ghosts, HOT LAP, SNIPEOUT, OVERCLOCK plus the skin, ACADEMY (11 drills, drone, gates, mine line), VERSUS (join, half keys, split HUD), the REPLAY scene, records | modes suite: each mode starts, plays, and ends with correct results; ghost save/load round-trips and plays back aligned (< 1 m error); Overclock zones advance and the run ends at 0 energy; the academy bot passes all drills; versus with 2 inputs makes 2 viewports and both finish; replay click-to-follow selects the clicked craft (feed a click at a projected position) |\\n| **M8** | Season and story | `08-data-season.js`, `09-data-story.js`, `78-season-ui.js` (hub, briefings, GP, ending, credits), saves, unlocks | season suite: the **scripted playthrough** (§7.4) of the whole season with the player bot; unlocks fire in order; save → reload → state equal; every dialog line references only defined vars; every event playable |\\n| **M9** | Sound | engine edit §2.7.4; `50-audio.js`: 6 songs and stings, the full SFX catalogue, engine hums, the music director (layers, final lap, overclock tempo), `SN.Voice` gibberish, announcer callouts, radio | audio suite (headless, no WebAudio): every song parses with no engine warnings and is ≥ 16 bars; each event type maps to an existing sound; `Voice.say` durations are > 0 and stable per word; the music layers react to race events (`audio.pos.layers`). 🔊 a human-free check: in the browser, record `audio.drift` stays < 10 ms and no audio errors |\\n| **M10** | Attract and dev | `85-attract.js`, `80-dev.js` (panel, cheats, sliders, reset, overlays, info) | flow: 10.0 s idle on the title → attract starts (not at 9.9 s); any of key/pad/click exits within 1 step; the attract shows ≥ 8 distinct weapons and ≥ 3 tracks across one loop (counted from events); dev: every slider changes `SN.Tune.T` and the sim responds (e.g., topSpeedMul 1.5 raises top speed); RESET ALL restores every default exactly; each cheat works |\\n| **M11** | AI Hub | `90-hub.js`, its own card, ghost send/receive, the session scene | hub suite (Node mock of `AIHub`, §7.6) and the **real harness** (§7.6): `players=2&auto=1`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, `…&scenario=host-leave`; `__hubCheck.pass === true` in each |\\n| **M12** | Polish and ship | scenery density, effects, juice (shake, flashes, rumble via `input.rumble`), the balance pass with the sliders, medal calibration (`tools/medals.mjs`), the About pages filled, `exit-interview.json`, the final bundle | the full `node tests/run.mjs` passes; `tools/bundle.mjs` passes its checks (no TODO, an identical hub client); `node engine/handoff/tools/check.mjs ../<bundle>.html` gives no errors (it will list the CDN files as external, which is expected); 📷 the final screenshot set (§7.7) |\",\"numLines\":120,\"startLine\":1585,\"totalLines\":2081}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01L78sMc52XE5nNFSaDTyY5J\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f\",\"uuid\":\"47af1671-3539-4ce4-8c34-a106f5f16327\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184337__xe162c9/work/OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-184337/package-lock.json","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":42,"lines":["+{","+  \"name\": \"operation-wolfpack\",","+  \"lockfileVersion\": 3,","+  \"requires\": true,","+  \"packages\": {","+    \"\": {","+      \"name\": \"operation-wolfpack\",","+      \"devDependencies\": {","+        \"playwright\": \"1.63.0\"","+      }","+    },","+    \"node_modules/playwright\": {","+      \"version\": \"1.63.0\",","+      \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/playwright/-/playwright-1.63.0.tgz\",","+      \"integrity\": \"sha512-+7ziBLidS4NaNCdt57SUDT+wYmmd5fmiQejUic/kb+YsYSCPyOOE9sebzMjNmQrsnNpDJqd4WHvV/8lfKfUDUg==\",","+      \"dev\": true,","+      \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",","+      \"dependencies\": {","+        \"playwright-core\": \"1.63.0\"","+      },","+      \"bin\": {","+        \"playwright\": \"cli.js\"","+      },","+      \"engines\": {","+        \"node\"