{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh8W9KBo5BG8f4PNodPx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stereo panning and storm wind are now in, so nothing from the plan is left out. All test suites pass on the final file, including the AI Hub harness rerun after the last sim changes.\n\n- **Stereo panning:** sound effects now play from their side of the screen: gunfire, explosions, enemy fire and the helicopter rotor. This needed one more engine edit, logged in `engine/CHANGES.md`. A new test checks that a sound on the left of the screen pans left and one on the right pans right.\n- **Wind:** the Op 6 storm, and Op 5 more lightly, now slants the rain, drifts smoke, embers and dust sideways, speeds up the windsock, and plays wind gusts. A test checks the smoke drift.\n\n**Tests on the final file:**\n\n| Suites | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Headless, including the whole-game playthrough | 618 passed |\n| Lint | 372 passed |\n| Bundle and exit-interview checks | 51 passed |\n| Browser (Chromium on the final file) | 16 passed |\n| AI Hub harness, all 5 configurations | 10 passed |\n\nAll with 0 failures. No servers of mine are still running.\n\n`OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-184337.html` and `exit-interview.json` are in the root. The interview's answers and the in-game About pages now include these changes.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:43:37\n- **Source:** Operation Wolf (Taito, 1987 arcade)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Light-gun rail shooter; first person on a scripted rail camera (Mode 7 depth view) with a free crosshair\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 full engine (Mode 7, Arcade, Shell modules; 5 small engine edits), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript in one HTML file; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests and the bundle\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native PS1/SNES pixel style: shaded HD Humanoid characters, vehicles and props written as engine shape data, painted Mode 7 floors and skies, pixel-art HUD and screens\n- **Animation:** The engine's character rig (walk/run, aim, throw, kneel, crouch, die, faces, portraits) plus custom poses: hands up, bound hands, panic, the officer's whistle, rocket on the shoulder, parachute. Rotors, wheels, toppling masts and the collapsing tower are animated in code.\n- **Audio:** All synthesized in code: about 50 sound effects panned by their place on screen, 13 original songs whose layers follow the action, gibberish (Animalese-style) voices per speaker, the wolf howl, storm wind gusts\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world co-op for 1–4 (the host runs the game, other players mirror it, with the game's own lobby card); local co-op for 1–4 with drop-in controllers\n- **Testing:** Headless scripted tests and bot play behind one command (prints failures plus a count), a whole-game bot playthrough, Playwright checks of the final file, the real AI Hub harness; screenshots for look only\n- **Research:** Planner: Wikipedia and arcade-history.com on Operation Wolf. Builder: none beyond the engine and hub docs.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** Cost and tokens unknown; session time about 1 hour 5 minutes (measured before the last two rounds of fixes, so the full session ran longer)\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 18.\n- **How many were critical?** 6:\n  - Knife throwers and mortar crews were silently replaced by projectile types with the same names.\n  - Enemies never attacked, because a timer started undefined.\n  - An endless reload loop with part-used magazines.\n  - The final gunship flew above the screen.\n  - A boss part was unhittable behind its own body.\n  - Continues replayed the same lost fight forever.\n- **Most helpful test:** The bot playthrough of each operation that reported damage taken by source.\n- **Least helpful test:** Screenshots of static menus; they found nothing a script hadn't.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Mode 7's `project` and `toFloor`: the same math draws the world and decides what a shot hits.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Character heights in world units aren't documented, so I measured them in a browser. `E.store` silently forgot everything where browser storage is blocked.\n- **Most important thing I built myself:** The light-gun loop: on-screen hit areas, the rail camera with holds, attack warnings and the bot.\n- **Hardest part:** Mode 7 draws on top of everything else, so the engine's lights and particles don't apply. The effects and the night darkness had to be my own.\n- **What I changed:**\n  - Dialog can call a function per typed letter (for the voices).\n  - Shell got a screen of setting rows, plus setting groups hidden from Settings (for the dev mode).\n  - PlayStation button symbols are the default.\n  - `E.store` keeps data for the visit when storage is blocked.\n  - Sound effects take a stereo pan.\n- **One change I'd make:** A first-person gallery mode for Mode 7 that keeps lighting, particles and hit picking.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** A clear deliverable plus a detailed plan to build from.\n- **Confusing:** The plan's file names (max effort, 17:47:46) differ from TASK.md's. TASK.md wins, but it costs a moment.\n- **Hardest:** The amount of content (six operations, six bosses, cutscenes, co-op and netcode) in one session.\n- **What I'd change:** Have the plan carry the exact deliverable names, or state that names always come from TASK.md."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":379,"cache_read_input_tokens":574495,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":379},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c87f55d5-27de-4595-aefb-732ca102ecfb","uuid":"986be45b-a28c-4c83-aada-725b4f1b3176","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:52:18.894Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh8W934GBdZNLTuJJzxP"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled .html and exit-interview.json exist, and the final reply has all four sections. But the feature condition is not evidenced. TASK.md asks for a 50-title brainstorm recorded by a real RNG run, plus a 'Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator' step, and PLAN.md's title choice relies on a planner's RNG run, not the builder's. The transcript shows no RNG run by the builder. Also, the final reply and interview say 'Date: 2026-11-03 18:43:37' while the transcript shows the session's own 'Date' drifts; more importantly, the 'Usage' field says session time was about 1 hour 5 minutes, which was measured before the final fixes and is admitted to be stale. The Stop condition's feature check is therefore not fully supported by transcript evidence, and the agent's own final reply concedes the usage figure is stale."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c87f55d5-27de-4595-aefb-732ca102ecfb","uuid":"17d74f63-93ff-4cbc-9e17-370ccf040cab","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:52:22.146Z","isSynthetic":true}
