{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh8YV6sLoDit2ez3B79z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the stale usage figure, but I did not re-pick the title.\n\n**Title:** I kept \"Operation Wolfpack\" on purpose. STAGE.md says to build \"using the title it gives\", meaning the plan's title. PLAN.md records that the planner brainstormed 50 titles and ran `python3 -c \"import secrets; print(secrets.randbelow(50) + 1)\"`, got 33, and says \"Don't pick again\". That was a real random-number-generator run, so the plan doesn't contradict TASK.md here. A second pick by me would contradict STAGE.md and could rename every deliverable.\n\n**Usage:** the session time is now 18:43:37 to 19:53, about 1 hour 10 minutes, in both `exit-interview.json` and the in-game About page. The date, 2026-11-03 18:43:37, is the start time TASK.md gives, so it stays as written.\n\n**Tests:** after the rebuild I reran only the lint and bundle checks, and they pass (372 and 51, 0 failed). Only that text changed, so I did not rerun the browser or AI Hub harness checks; both passed on the build just before (16 and 10 checks).\n\nThe bundled .html is in the root, and the exit interview parses with every field filled.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:43:37\n- **Source:** Operation Wolf (Taito, 1987 arcade)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (its title, \"Operation Wolfpack\", was #33 of 50, picked by the planner with `secrets.randbelow`)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Light-gun rail shooter; first person on a scripted rail camera (Mode 7 depth view) with a free crosshair\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 full engine (Mode 7, Arcade, Shell modules; 5 small engine edits), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript in one HTML file; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests and the bundle\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native PS1/SNES pixel style: shaded HD Humanoid characters, vehicles and props written as engine shape data, painted Mode 7 floors and skies, pixel-art HUD and screens\n- **Animation:** The engine's character rig (walk/run, aim, throw, kneel, crouch, die, faces, portraits) plus custom poses: hands up, bound hands, panic, the officer's whistle, rocket on the shoulder, parachute. Rotors, wheels, toppling masts and the collapsing tower are animated in code.\n- **Audio:** All synthesized in code: about 50 sound effects panned by where they are on screen, 13 original songs whose layers follow the action, gibberish (Animalese-style) voices per speaker, the wolf howl, storm wind gusts\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world co-op for 1–4 (the host runs the game, other players mirror it, with the game's own lobby card); local co-op for 1–4 with drop-in controllers\n- **Testing:** Headless scripted tests and bot play behind one command (prints failures plus a count), a whole-game bot playthrough, Playwright checks of the final file, the real AI Hub harness; screenshots for look only\n- **Research:** Planner: Wikipedia and arcade-history.com on Operation Wolf. Builder: none beyond the engine and hub docs.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** Cost and tokens unknown; session time about 1 hour 10 minutes (18:43:37 to 19:53)\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 18.\n- **How many were critical?** 6:\n  - Knife throwers and mortar crews were silently replaced by projectile types with the same names.\n  - Enemies never attacked, because a timer started undefined.\n  - An endless reload loop with part-used magazines.\n  - The final gunship flew above the screen.\n  - A boss part was unhittable behind its own body.\n  - Continues replayed the same lost fight forever.\n- **Most helpful test:** The bot playthrough of each operation that reported damage taken by source.\n- **Least helpful test:** Screenshots of static menus; they found nothing a script hadn't.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Mode 7's `project` and `toFloor`: the same math draws the world and decides what a shot hits.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Character heights in world units aren't documented, so I measured them in a browser. `E.store` silently forgot everything where browser storage is blocked.\n- **Most important thing I built myself:** The light-gun loop: on-screen hit areas, the rail camera with holds, attack warnings and the bot.\n- **Hardest part:** Mode 7 draws on top of everything else, so the engine's lights and particles don't apply. The effects and the night darkness had to be my own.\n- **What I changed:**\n  - Dialog can call a function per typed letter (for the voices).\n  - Shell got a screen of setting rows, plus setting groups hidden from Settings (for the dev mode).\n  - PlayStation button symbols are the default.\n  - `E.store` keeps data for the visit when storage is blocked.\n  - Sound effects take a stereo pan.\n- **One change I'd make:** A first-person gallery mode for Mode 7 that keeps lighting, particles and hit picking.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** A clear deliverable plus a detailed plan to build from.\n- **Confusing:** The plan's file names (max effort, 17:47:46) differ from TASK.md's. TASK.md wins, but it costs a moment.\n- **Hardest:** The amount of content (six operations, six bosses, cutscenes, co-op and netcode) in one session.\n- **What I'd change:** Have the plan carry the exact deliverable names, or state that names always come from TASK.md."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":521,"cache_read_input_tokens":577816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":521},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c87f55d5-27de-4595-aefb-732ca102ecfb","uuid":"1dc8616b-3b96-452d-94fd-cea2969531b9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:52:50.140Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh8YUq152R7jxzGUuygb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The transcript shows the bundled HTML and exit-interview.json exist and parse, and the final reply includes all four sections. But the feature condition is not evidenced. TASK.md requires the builder to silently brainstorm 50 titles and pick one with a real RNG run (or the plan's RNG run). The transcript shows no builder RNG run; the title 'Operation Wolfpack' is taken from PLAN.md, whose RNG run was done by the planner, and the agent explicitly declined to re-pick. The final reply also states that the browser and AI Hub harness checks were not rerun after the last text edit, so the most recent test state is not fully verified, though the earlier runs passed. Without an RNG-backed title selection performed in this session, the 'every feature in TASK.md' requirement is not shown to hold."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c87f55d5-27de-4595-aefb-732ca102ecfb","uuid":"f87498ae-9c32-44cf-8770-f3a661497bef","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:52:52.028Z","isSynthetic":true}
