{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh8m1Cwb95S52MgKXVEc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I cancelled the leftover scheduled wake-up (job `c523fc4e`); it was a session-only timer from waiting on the test run, so nothing is left scheduled.\n\nI've again kept the title \"Operation Wolfpack\" and not run my own random pick. STAGE.md tells me to build \"using the title it gives\". The plan records a real random pick by the planner: 50 titles brainstormed, `secrets.randbelow(50) + 1` returned 33, and it says \"Don't pick again\". TASK.md's rule (brainstorm 50, pick with a real random-number generator) was therefore met, and the two files don't conflict. A fresh pick by me would contradict STAGE.md and the plan, and would force renaming every deliverable. If you want a pick made in this session anyway, say so and I'll do the draw and the renames.\n\nEverything else is done:\n- The single .html file and `exit-interview.json` are in the root, and the interview parses with every field answered.\n- The source has no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n- The last runs on the final file all pass:\n\n| Suite | Checks passed | Failed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Headless suites | 618 | 0 |\n| Lint | 372 | 0 |\n| Bundle | 51 | 0 |\n| Browser | 16 | 0 |\n| AI Hub harness (5 configurations) | 10 | 0 |\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:43:37\n- **Source:** Operation Wolf (Taito, 1987 arcade)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (its title was the planner's random pick, #33 of 50, with `secrets.randbelow`)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Light-gun rail shooter; first person on a scripted rail camera (Mode 7 depth view) with a free crosshair\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 full engine (Mode 7, Arcade, Shell; 5 small engine edits), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript in one HTML file; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests and the bundle\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native PS1/SNES pixel style: shaded HD Humanoid